@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam roundcorner 12
left to right direction
title PDF presentation — generated rendering versus uploaded delivery
actor Visitor
rectangle "PublicResumeController\nActive resume, current grant and mode checks" as Gate
rectangle "Generated path\nResume + profile + section relationships" as Data #DBEAFE
artifact "public/resume-pdf.blade.php\nPDF-specific HTML/CSS\nStructured content and named links\nMonth/year date presentation" as Template
rectangle "DOMPDF\nA4 portrait layout\nFonts, wrapping and page breaks" as Engine
artifact "Generated resume PDF\nIdentity/title-based filename" as Generated #DCFCE7
rectangle "Uploaded path\nExisting private-storage PDF\nNo template rendering or content regeneration" as Upload #FEF3C7
artifact "Uploaded resume PDF\nIdentity/title-based filename" as Original #DCFCE7
Visitor --> Gate : request PDF download
Gate --> Data : generated/both permitted
Data --> Template : Blade view data
Template --> Engine : rendered HTML/CSS
Engine --> Generated : PDF download response
Gate --> Upload : uploaded/both permitted
Upload --> Original : private disk download response
note bottom of Gate
 Missing/inactive resume: 404.
 Missing protected grant: password redirect.
 Disabled requested mode: 403.
 Missing uploaded file: 404.
end note
note bottom of Engine
 Public HTML uses a separate Blade template and browser engine.
 Browser screenshots do not verify PDF layout.
 Use short/long synthetic fixtures to check page breaks,
 clipping, fonts, images and links.
end note
@enduml